WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:02.840
(relaxing music)

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.989
- [Narrator] Reaching up towards the sky,

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:06.989
these 3,000 pillars stand
tall from the valley below

00:00:06.989 --> 00:00:10.239
to make a towering forest of sandstone.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.129
The Zhangjiajie National
Forest Park is located

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:19.426
in the west Hunan Province of China

00:00:19.426 --> 00:00:21.619
and is over 600 miles
away from the major cities

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:23.619
of Shanghai and Beijing.

00:00:26.761 --> 00:00:28.289
Fans of James Cameron's Avatar

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:30.319
may find these rock pillars familiar.

00:00:30.319 --> 00:00:32.153
They were the inspiration
behind the mythical world

00:00:32.153 --> 00:00:34.070
of Pandora in the film.

00:00:34.948 --> 00:00:37.858
These pillars resulted from
weather over many years.

00:00:37.858 --> 00:00:39.388
A combination of the changing seasons

00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:40.728
and the plants that grow on them

00:00:40.728 --> 00:00:44.999
have contributed to their
individual and unique shapes.

00:00:44.999 --> 00:00:46.456
Although the seasons change,

00:00:46.456 --> 00:00:48.279
the weather is moist all year round,

00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:50.347
which results in dense foliage.

00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:54.514
In fact, 98% of the park
is covered in vegetation.

00:00:55.657 --> 00:00:56.814
There are hiking trails available

00:00:56.814 --> 00:00:58.397
to see this incredible forest.

00:00:58.397 --> 00:01:00.086
However, as James Cameron knows,

00:01:00.086 --> 00:01:04.169
nothing compares to
experiencing it from the sky.

